.TH SOX-NOISE 1 "2026-08-04" "1.0" "Sox Noise Manual"
.SH NAME
sox-noise \- graphical and command-line utility for generating white/pink/brown noise
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sox-noise
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ COLOR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sox-noise
is a noise generator GUI powered by Sound eXchange (SoX).
.PP
Launching the executable with no arguments opens the main application window.
The program also has a command-line interface: it can be used to launch the
GUI pre-configured with the options given, to run headless (see
.B \-\-hide
below), or to render noise directly to a file or audio device without ever
opening a window. When run from a terminal, it also prints SoX's own
live encoding/progress output for debugging purposes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.RI [ COLOR ]
The "color" of noise to generate. One of:
.BR brown ", " pink ", " white ", " tpdf .
.TP
.B \-h\fR,\fB \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ CONFIG
Configuration file location (default: \fI~/.config/sox-noise/default.sxn\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-play
Start playing on open.
.TP
.BI \-\-volume \ VOLUME
Playback volume [1-120].
.TP
.BI \-\-band\-center \ BAND_CENTER
Band-pass filter center frequency [1-2000] (Hz).
.TP
.BI \-\-band\-width \ BAND_WIDTH
Band-pass filter width [1-1000].
.TP
.B \-\-effects
Show effects options.
.TP
.BI \-\-reverb \ REVERB
Reverb amount [0-100]. Small amounts make the noise sound more natural.
.TP
.BI \-\-tremolo\-speed \ TREMOLO_SPEED
Periodically raise and lower the volume [0-10] (cycles per duration).
.TP
.BI \-\-tremolo\-depth \ TREMOLO_DEPTH
Tremolo intensity [0-100].
.TP
.BI \-\-lowpass \ LOWPASS
Lowpass filter width. Disable with 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-duration \ DURATION
How many seconds of noise to generate before looping (default: 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-fade \ FADE
How long to fade in/out on loop, in seconds. Prevents clicking/popping
(default: 0.005).
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Show an icon in the system tray.
.TP
.B \-\-hide
Don't show the window.
.TP
.BI \-\-save \ SAVE
Save sound to the given filename instead of (or in addition to) playing it.
.TP
.BI \-\-output \ {pulse,alsa,wav,sox,default}
Output device/format.
.TP
.B \-\-spectrogram
Show the spectrogram.
.TP
.BI \-\-extras \ EXTRAS \ [ EXTRAS \ ...]
Extra arguments to pass through to \fBsox\fR(1) directly.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the application and package version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sox-noise \-\-play
Launch the GUI and immediately start playing the default noise. This
also prints the underlying
.B sox
invocation and its live progress meter to the terminal, e.g.:
.PP
.RS
.EX
\&\ ===> sox \-c2 \-\-null \-d synth 0:60 brownnoise band \-n 500.0 500.0 \e
    tremolo 0.03333333333333333 30.0 reverb 20.0 vol 0.8 fade q 0.005 0:60 0.005 repeat \-
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sox-noise/default.sxn
Default configuration file, loaded unless overridden with \fB\-\-config\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sox (1)
